Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes, reversible typed-record packing, and a bz2 fallback for other inputs. Verified byte-identical restoration of corpus_hard.txt and additional edge cases. The compressed file is 16,786 bytes versus 44,267 original bytes and 22,390 bytes for default zlib: a 62.0801% size reduction. Registered fitness.py as the assay, improved through scored variants, and confirmed identical fitness across three final runs.